We now know how many successful heists each squirrel had, out of 150.

Let's visualise how many squirrels have each number of successful heists - i.e. how many of our 1000 squirrels stole seeds once, twice, three times etc.

First, we need to convert our vector into a data frame. We can do this by using the function `tibble()` and assigning the vector to a column.

::: {.callout-note #copy-libraries2 .copycode}

### Include this code

Include the following as an R code chunk in your `squirrels.qmd` Quarto file.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
df_squirrels <- tibble("N_Successful_Heists" = combined_successes)
gt(head(df_squirrels))
```

